WEBVTT

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.840
A doorway to dreams
is being opened somewhere.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.670
What?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.680
Something happened between
you and Souseiseki, didn't it?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.220
Please tell me about it,
 Suiseiseki.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.190
I had no idea.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.920
Poor Souseiseki.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:00.660
It would not be strange for Souseiseki
to open a doorway to dreams, but...

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.200
It sounds rather suspicious.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.170
What?

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.320
I mean Suigintou.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:10.170
To what purpose did she
appear before Suiseiseki?

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.000
You don't mean...

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.210
The N Field...

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.590
Wait.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.090
You needn't concern yourselves.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.970
This is a problem between 
Souseiseki and me.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.200
I cannot trouble everyone...

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.570
After all the trouble
you've put us through so far...

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.500
talk about a rare show of restraint.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.320
Jun!

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.280
Just quit it.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.570
It's creepy.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.440
Shut up, you!

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.440
Jun is telling you to put us
through trouble this time as well.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.690
Jun is my servant.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.450
I told you that he is not 
a bad human, didn't I?

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.820
Oh, fine.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.820
Hurry up and come along, you!

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.830
She sure is never at a loss for words.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.390
Souseiseki...

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.540
Cage

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.820
Nothing has changed.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.400
What about her?

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.060
She has always been asleep,
ever since I first came here.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.990
Hey, this is a normal house.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.570
If we get caught, 
that's breaking and entering...

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.660
Hey, this is bad.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.560
This one won't wake up.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.900
Oh! A doorway to dreams!

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.180
Be quiet!

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.170
Just as we thought...

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.580
Let's go.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.880
Um, well, pardon the intrusion.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.670
Up we go.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.640
This place is just packed with clocks.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.420
It's the same as how your dream
was full of minicars.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.380
Darkness and broken clocks...

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.920
This man's heart is...

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.040
Yay! A cuckoo clock!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.380
Oh, I get it.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.430
Hey, that's not it!

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.260
I see Souseiseki!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.670
That's...

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.000
Hey, hold it, you!

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.010
We seem to have lost sight of her.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.460
She is so quick on her feet.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.520
Souseiseki?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.380
Souseiseki!

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.830
We'll get her out right away.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:27.920
Jun?

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.060
Right.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.910
Souseiseki!

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.910
She seems to be unconscious.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.110
Darn you!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.280
Wake up!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.520
Hey, there are gentler ways
of waking someone up.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.250
That hurts.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.760
Thank goodness!
 Souseiseki!

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.800
Suiseiseki...

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.700
Shinku...
 all of you...

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:03.000
Tell me, Souseiseki,
 where's Lempicka?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.540
Might this be what you are looking for?

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:12.970
Suigintou!

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:18.240
Being kind to the elderly
certainly has its benefits.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.740
I got this easily, 
thanks to that.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.250
What kind of dirty trick
did you use to get in here?

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.480
Oh, please.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.300
The one who opened the 
doorway to dreams...

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.260
...is your beloved sister.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.220
She knew that Grandfather
was trying to trap her in his dreams...

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.670
...and she still opened the doorway.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.270
Isn't that right?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.190
Souseiseki!

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.770
You'd go that far for that
pain-in-the-neck old geezer?

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.480
Don't speak badly of the master.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.740
You're still talking 
like you're half-asleep?

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.820
I will slap you awake all over again!

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.720
Calm down, Suiseiseki.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:05.060
But with only Lempicka, I feel like
I'm missing a little something.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:11.130
Say, Suiseiseki, 
give Sui Dream to me too.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.260
That's quite enough.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.740
Return Lempicka, Suigintou.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:23.770
You are so thoroughly stupid, Shinku.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:28.340
You think you have any chance
of winning in this world?

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.520
This world is the world 
of Grandfather's dreams.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.520
It's incredibly kind to me.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:42.970
Shinku!

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:43.460
Hold on!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:47.900
Jun!

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.540
Hina's gonna help too!

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:03.030
Suiseiseki, 
leave Suigintou to us.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.250
Take Jun and Souseiseki
and get away from here.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.600
Got it! 
I understand!

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:10.420
The doorway to dreams!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.020
It vanished...

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:19.120
The master has no intention 
of letting us escape.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.160
This way!

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.640
Shinku...

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.880
Just do your best to crawl along,
making your clumsy way around.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.310
It's huge.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.090
Is this the old man's tree?

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.930
What the hell do you 
think you're looking at?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:25.960
This is a branch.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.780
A branch 
of the World Tree.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:28.590
A branch?

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:34.520
All dreams are linked through branches
to a single giant tree...

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.440
...the World Tree.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.480
Though dreams never intermingle
with one another...

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.620
...through the intervention of
the World Tree branches...

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.940
Sorry, could you explain 
that in under 30 words?

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:46.570
Oh, fine.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.680
I'll stoop to the level of
the runt's intelligence here.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.020
These branches connect the dreams
of those who share an emotional bond.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.520
Emotional?

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:20.080
The emotional connection 
is half-withered.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.000
Master...

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.960
Can we really cross this thing?

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.460
It will hold the weight of Rose Dolls
with no problem.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.090
What about me?

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.510
Hey!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:38.760
Damn it!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:45.470
What the...

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.300
We are entering the dream world.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.520
Huh? There's nothing here.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.250
It is because her heart is empty.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.690
This is a very sad place.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:15.140
They lost their only son,
Kazuki-kun, in a car accident.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:21.840
The master's wife has been asleep
ever since then.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.640
I'm sure something must be
happening to his wife's tree.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.340
So...

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.030
If we free the tree...

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.650
...the old woman should wake
from her long slumber.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:36.200
The old man is obsessed with you
due to his deep loneliness.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:40.660
Saving the old woman
will save the old man's spirit.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:41.800
Darn it!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.530
Why must I faithfully recite 
what's on your mind?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:46.830
You inarticulate doll!

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:52.530
But I want you to find a new master
and find happiness.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.070
We've come this far!

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.540
There is nothing left 
but to do this now!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.540
Suiseiseki!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.110
We will all split up and look for
the old woman's tree.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:04.490
Human, hurry up and start sniffing
around for its scent!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.630
What am I, 
a truffle pig?

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:07.720
Stop it.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:10.480
Please, just stop it.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.270
Who...

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.810
Kazuki-kun!

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:39.350
Kazuki-kun...

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.790
Don't look for the tree.

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:45.350
Mother says she doesn't want to wake up.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.350
Why not?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.360
Because I'm in this world.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:55.370
There's nothing here.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.630
No scary cars.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.860
No sad happenings.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.640
Mother wants to live with 
me in this quiet world...

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.960
...just the two of us forever.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:07.410
Forever, never to be hurt by anyone.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:08.870
But...

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:15.250
Then what about the old man?

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.470
Sure, losing you must 
have come as a shock...

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.580
...but to turn away from reality

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.060
and shut herself in the 
safe world of dreams is...

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:29.700
Shut away... 
in a safe world...

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.060
Human...

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.590
But...

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.570
But Mother...

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.020
Your father is lonely too.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.810
Your mother is still alive.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.820
You have to let her go 
back to the real world.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.340
Father...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.320
Mother...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.190
Hold it right there!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.230
Take this!

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.210
We did it!

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.710
What the...

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.100
Suigintou!

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.180
What's happened to 
Shinku and Hina-Ichigo?

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:32.300
We must run away for now.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.690
Sui Dream!

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.070
Let's hurry up and go!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.950
Come on, human!
 You fly too!

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.630
Right.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.470
Wait, what about Kazuki-kun?

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.880
Kazuki-kun...

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.660
Ow!

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:07.420
We must hurry and close the
doorway to dreams or Suigintou...

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.970
Welcome back.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.970
I was getting tired of waiting.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.700
What did you do to 
Shinku and Hina-Ichigo?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.320
Who knows?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.210
Maybe they've gotten 
lost in the dream world.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.710
Sui Dream!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.550
It's no use.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:43.860
You have no master...

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.820
so you can only use your powers
in the dream world.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:47.390
Furthermore...

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:54.930
Souseiseki!

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:56.770
Furthermore...

00:15:56.770 --> 00:16:00.040
a doll robbed of Lempicka 
is nothing but junk!

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:14.450
Quietly hand over Sui Dream, Suiseiseki.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.720
I would prefer not to 
resort to violence.

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.960
You think... 
these miserable feathers can...

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:26.200
Human!

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.050
Lempicka!

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:33.770
Suiseiseki, run!

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:41.510
Human!

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:42.750
No!

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.250
Don't! 
Move aside!

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:52.990
I'm not so degenerate that
I would need a human's help!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.260
Hurry up and move!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.590
Human, if you don't, you'll...

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:01.220
I'm not so degenerate either...

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.250
that I'd stand aside 
when you're so weak!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:04.770
Human...

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.270
I wonder how long you'll be able to
keep up that bravado.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:14.260
Human, you mustn't!
 You have to run!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.480
Lempicka, stop it!

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.980
Lempicka belongs to me now.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.490
It's no use, Souseiseki.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:25.490
Human!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:30.180
Jun!

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:35.930
Suigintou!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.670
I'll give you my damn Sui Dream!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.900
Suiseiseki...

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:43.870
So stop hurting Jun!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.880
Good girl.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.420
No...

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.120
Don't, Suiseiseki!

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.160
Sui Dream...

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.120
Suiseiseki!

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.190
Good girl.

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:24.910
We can't get back.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.020
I can't walk any more.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.560
Oh, it's Kun-kun!

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:38.060
Kun-kun!

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:41.530
Kun-kun! Kun-kun!

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.900
I'll show you the way out.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.400
Kun-kun talked...

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:50.940
You...

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.910
In exchange, would you tell
my mother and father something?

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:59.910
That no matter where they are,
I'll always be with them.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:01.910
You're sure?

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.370
I'll be okay.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.100
Kazuki!

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.890
Kazuki!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.920
Kazuki!

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:24.570
Kazuki!

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:25.870
Kazuki, where are you?

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:31.170
I see.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:32.880
So we've lost Sui Dream too.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:36.880
But, but I'm glad everyone's safe.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.230
Yeah.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:42.050
Are you in here, Kazuki?

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:46.090
Master...

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:48.380
Kazuki!

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.870
Who are you?

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.100
Oh, um, pleased to make 
your acquaintance.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.100
Have you come to take 
Kazuki away from me?

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.750
What? No, I haven't.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:02.110
I don't need more troublesome...

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.110
Shut up!

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:37.330
Matsu!

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.980
Dear...

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.130
Kazuki...

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.460
Kazuki?

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:00.900
Mystical Nupopo Doll.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:04.080
Buy now and get another 
one for free, huh?

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:09.890
This token deal completely ignores that
they could've just sold two to start with.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:10.870
I like it.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:14.140
A sneak attack from 
behind, you rotten doll?

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.300
Wrong.
 It's Hina.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:19.790
Oh, right.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.650
She's not around
 anymore, is she?

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:24.650
Do you miss her, Jun?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:26.890
As if!

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:30.690
I'm glad we got rid of a noisy one!

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.380
Here you are, Grandma. Tea.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.190
Thank you, Dear.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:41.720
Could I have another 
cup too, Souseiseki?

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:42.400
Certainly.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.120
I swear...

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:45.720
Hot!

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:48.410
Let me see that, Suiseiseki.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:53.380
It cools down nicely if you do this.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:54.920
That's elementary!

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:58.080
Not that I knew that...

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:43.780
Everyone, it was good of you to come.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:45.960
Please relax and think 
of this as your own home.

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:46.880
It's my home.

00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:50.320
Jun, I will give you an
honorable service to perform.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:52.610
Go on, hurry up and make tea.

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.780
Prepare some sweets as well.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.670
Sheesh! 
What is this all of a sudden?

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:57.730
